<h2>Why careful claim documentation pays off</h2>
<p>An insurer pays for what it can see and verify. The claim documentation checklist above is built around that simple fact: the more clearly you can show what was damaged, when it happened, and what it takes to fix it, the less room there is for disagreement later about the date of loss, old wear and tear, or items that never made it into the estimate.</p>
<p>The hard part is that evidence does not last. Rain washes hail marks off a roof, wet drywall gets torn out, and debris goes to the curb. In busy years the Hays County NOAA record fills up quickly (15 hail reports in 2024 alone), so dated photos also help tie damage to the right storm. Work through the list while the damage is still visible.</p>

